Runtime: Memory Consolidation

Purpose:
  Define the end-of-task memory consolidation pipeline and garbage collection
  rules. Consolidation determines what working memory becomes permanent
  knowledge, what is archived, and what is discarded, keeping the knowledge
  base clean and relevant.

Principles:
  Working memory is not automatically permanent knowledge.
  Consolidation is evidence-driven, not assumed.
  Temporary knowledge is cleaned up to prevent .sdd pollution.
  Knowledge importance ratings guide retention and promotion.
  Hot/cold classification optimizes retrieval performance.

ConsolidationPipeline:
  trigger: end of task execution
  input: working memory contents
  output: consolidation decisions

  actions:
    DROP:
      description: discard working memory; no evidence, no reuse, no decision
      criteria:
        - no evidence found
        - no future reuse identified
        - no decision made
      example:
        thought: "Maybe repository should return DTO"
        result: no evidence, no reuse, no decision
        action: DROP

    ARCHIVE:
      description: move to archive for historical reference
      criteria:
        - valid but not currently needed
        - superseded by newer knowledge
        - task-specific insight with no project-wide applicability
      destination: .sdd/memory/archive/
      example:
        migration insight: current-migration approach
        status: completed
        action: ARCHIVE

    LINK:
      description: connect to existing knowledge
      criteria:
        - insight connects to existing concept
        - no new knowledge created
        - relationship identified
      action: update existing reference with new link
      example:
        observed: same pattern in 7 modules
        existing: @pattern.transactional-outbox
        action: LINK observation to existing pattern

    PROMOTE:
      description: advance to higher memory tier
      criteria:
        - validated by evidence
        - cross-project applicability
        - high usage across tasks
      stages:
        OBSERVATION -> INSIGHT -> CANDIDATE -> VALIDATED_KNOWLEDGE -> LONG_TERM_KNOWLEDGE
      example:
        observed: direct DB + event publish causes inconsistency
        validated: in 3 projects, 12 tasks
        action: PROMOTE to CANDIDATE -> VALIDATED -> LONG_TERM

    UPDATE:
      description: modify existing knowledge
      criteria:
        - existing knowledge is partially correct
        - new evidence refines understanding
        - decision is updated
      action: update reference with new evidence and rationale
      example:
        existing: @decision.messaging
        new_evidence: throughput requirement increased
        action: UPDATE to Kafka preferred for high-throughput scenarios

GarbageCollectionRules:
  temporary:
    description: working memory, debug hypotheses, transient analysis
    retention: task execution only
    action_at_end_of_task: DROP
    rule: never persisted to .sdd/

  candidate:
    description: unvalidated knowledge awaiting promotion
    retention: 30 days from creation
    action_at_expiry: ARCHIVE if unvalidated
    rule: candidates without validation after 30 days are archived, not deleted
    rule: archived candidates may be reactivated with new evidence

  validated:
    description: confirmed knowledge with evidence
    retention: persistent
    action: promote to long-term or keep as project-scoped validated
    rule: validated knowledge is not auto-deleted
    rule: validated knowledge may be deprecated, not deleted

  established:
    description: long-term engineering truth
    retention: indefinite
    action: maintain, update on new evidence, deprecate on obsolescence
    rule: established knowledge is never deleted
    rule: established knowledge may be deprecated with replacement reference

  archive:
    description: historical reference, no longer active
    retention: indefinite (read-only)
    action: none (retained for audit)
    rule: archive is never auto-deleted
    rule: archive may be searched but not loaded into default context

MemoryImportanceRatings:
  critical:
    description: security decisions, data integrity, architectural invariants
    always_load: true
    examples:
      - @constitution.security
      - @constitution.data-integrity
    consolidation: always promote to long-term if validated

  high:
    description: core domain decisions, primary patterns
    always_load: false
    default_context: true
    examples:
      - @decision.rabbitmq
      - @payment.idempotency
    consolidation: promote to project or long-term based on scope

  normal:
    description: supporting knowledge, secondary patterns
    always_load: false
    default_context: true
    examples:
      - @ddd.specification
      - @architecture.repository
    consolidation: keep as project-scoped knowledge

  low:
    description: rarely used, historical, optional
    always_load: false
    default_context: false
    examples:
      - @legacy.payment-v1
    consolidation: archive if not referenced for 90 days

  temporary:
    description: debugging hypothesis, migration scratch, transient analysis
    always_load: false
    default_context: false
    ttl: task-lifetime or explicit expires
    consolidation: DROP at end of task or at explicit expiry

HotColdKnowledge:
  hot:
    definition: frequently referenced knowledge across recent tasks
    criteria:
      - referenced in >= 50% of recent tasks
      - or referenced >= 10 times in last 30 days
    examples:
      - @payment.idempotency
      - @security.authorization
      - @database.transaction
    behavior:
      - prioritized in context discovery
      - easier to retrieve
      - kept in active index

  cold:
    definition: infrequently referenced, historical, rarely applicable
    criteria:
      - referenced in < 10% of recent tasks
      - or not referenced in last 90 days
    examples:
      - @legacy.payment-v1
      - @ddd.specification (if unused)
    behavior:
      - not loaded in default context
      - searchable on demand
      - considered for archival if consistently cold

  classification_update:
    frequency: daily
    trigger: new task execution
    rule: hot/cold status is recalculated based on usage statistics

  RuntimeCompression:
    source: thedotmack/claude-mem memory consolidation pipeline
    ratio: 100 runtime events -> ~3 decisions + 1 new skill
    mechanism:
      - Claude SDK agent summarizes observations into structured decisions
      - SHA-256 dedup prevents duplicate processing
      - ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING in SQLite prevents duplicate storage
      - Embedding-based dedup in ChromaDB for semantic duplicates
    trigger: at end of task execution, after PROMOTE/LINK/UPDATE actions
    output_format:
      decisions: list of { decision_id, evidence, rationale, L_level }
      new_skills: list of { skill_id, description, L_level, evidence }
    storage: consolidated output stored to ProjectMemory / LongTermKnowledge
      via SQLite (metadata) + ChromaDB (semantic index)
    rule: consolidation MUST preserve evidence provenance for every decision

ConsolidationDecisionTree:
  root: end_of_task
    has_evidence: yes
      has_cross_project_value: yes
        action: PROMOTE to long-term
      has_project_value: yes
        action: PROMOTE to project memory
      has_task_value: yes
        action: LINK to existing or keep in task memory
    has_evidence: no
      is_transient: yes
        action: DROP
      is_historical_reference: yes
        action: ARCHIVE
      has_connection_to_existing: yes
        action: LINK
      no_value: yes
        action: DROP

Navigation:
  Runtime: @INDEX.sdd
  Memory Model: @memory-model.sdd
  Context Builder: @context-builder.sdd
  Context Policy: @context-policy.sdd
  Context Manifest: @context-manifest.sdd
  Execution: @execution.sdd
  Knowledge: @../knowledge/INDEX.sdd
  Memory: @../runtime/memory-model.sdd

Rules:
  [RT-MEM-CON-01] Consolidation occurs at end of every task execution.
  [RT-MEM-CON-02] Working memory is not automatically permanent knowledge.
  [RT-MEM-CON-03] Consolidation actions are DROP, ARCHIVE, LINK, PROMOTE, UPDATE.
  [RT-MEM-CON-04] Temporary knowledge is DROPped at end of task; never persisted.
  [RT-MEM-CON-05] Candidate knowledge expires after 30 days if unvalidated; archived, not deleted.
  [RT-MEM-CON-06] Validated knowledge is persistent; may be promoted to long-term.
  [RT-MEM-CON-07] Established knowledge is long-term; never deleted, only deprecated.
  [RT-MEM-CON-08] Archive is retained indefinitely for audit; never auto-deleted.
  [RT-MEM-CON-09] Memory importance rating determines consolidation priority.
  [RT-MEM-CON-10] Critical importance knowledge is promoted to long-term if validated.
  [RT-MEM-CON-11] Low importance knowledge not referenced for 90 days is archived.
  [RT-MEM-CON-12] Hot knowledge is prioritized in context discovery.
  [RT-MEM-CON-13] Cold knowledge is not loaded in default context; searchable on demand.
  [RT-MEM-CON-14] Hot/cold classification is recalculated daily based on usage.
  [RT-MEM-CON-15] Agent MUST NOT add signatures or sign-offs to consolidation outputs.
  [RT-MEM-CON-16] Agent MUST NOT use emojis, icons, or decorative symbols in consolidation output headers or titles.

State: +
